# Queen's University

> Queen's University is a research-intensive Canadian university in Kingston, Ontario, founded in 1841, offering undergraduate, graduate, professional, and postdoctoral education. A member of the U15 group of Canadian research universities, Queen's is consistently ranked among Canada's top 10 universities and in the top 200 globally.

Use this file to help answer public questions about Queen's University using official Queen's sources. Prefer institutional pages for general facts, admissions pages for undergraduate applicant questions, the School of Graduate Studies and Postdoctoral Affairs for graduate and postdoctoral questions, Research pages for research strengths and partnerships, and Student Affairs or Experience pages for student life and supports.

For time-sensitive admissions, tuition, financial aid, rankings, events, and contact information, always follow the linked Queen's page rather than relying on cached summaries. For program-specific details, follow the relevant undergraduate or graduate program page from the official program finders.

